  "vectorbt_accessor_kurtosis_convention": {
    "family_cases_measured": 7,
    "max_abs_dsr_gap": 8.704511321973134e-05,
    "finding": "vectorbt's accessor feeds excess kurtosis (scipy's fisher=True default) into a Pearson-kurtosis formula. On per-period hourly Sharpes the SR**2 term it scales is tiny, so the measured DSR gap on these real cases is small; it grows with the square of the per-period Sharpe. Recorded as a vectorbt defect, not an ARGUS advantage: ARGUS's gate takes kurtosis from its caller and cannot tell which convention it got."
